    "evidence": "INV-2207's five line totals each recompute correctly (6 x 24.50 = 147.00; 200 x 0.45 = 90.00; 2 x 38.00 = 76.00; 3 x 12.80 = 38.40; 1 x 15.00 = 15.00), but they sum to 366.40, not the 376.40 subtotal the invoice states. VAT at 20% on 366.40 is 73.28, so the sum of the line items plus 20% VAT is 439.68 - not the 451.68 total due. The stated total therefore exceeds its own line items plus VAT by 12.00 (a 10.00 overstatement of the subtotal, carried through VAT). The claim that 451.68 equals the line items plus 20% VAT does not hold: 451.68 implies a base of 376.40, which is 10.00 more than the line items sum to. Delivery (line 5, 15.00) is included as a line item; excluding it gives 351.40 + 20% = 421.68, also not 451.68. Uncertainty: the invoice document is the only evidence in the case, so this rests on the line items and figures as printed.",
